==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
The Icelandic pronoun continues {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|ek|lang=non}}, from {{proto|Germanic|ek|lang=is}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|éǵh₂|lang=is}}. The pronoun is attested, in [[w:Proto-Norse|proto-Norse]] inscriptions, since at least the 3rd century.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/jɛɣ/|lang=is}}
*: {{audio|Ég.ogg|audio}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|personal pronoun}}

# [[I#Personal pronoun|I]] {{qualifier|first-person singular pronoun}}
#* '''1584''', ''[[w:Guðbrandsbiblía|Guðbrandsbiblía]]'', Genesis 1.29 (orthography as in the [http://books.google.com/books?id=jicVAAAAYAAJ&dq=%22gef%20ykkur%20alls%20konar%22&pg=PA6#v=onepage&q=%22gef%20ykkur%20alls%20konar%22&f=false 1899 printing] and the [http://books.google.com/books?id=etkUAAAAYAAJ&dq=%22gef%20ykkur%20alls%20konar%22&pg=PP10#v=onepage&q=%22gef%20ykkur%20alls%20konar%22&f=false 1908 printing]):
#*: Og Guð sagði: sjá, '''eg''' gef ykkur alls konar sáðberandi jurtir {{...}}
#*:: Then God said, “'''I''' give you every seed-bearing plant {{...}}” (''NIV'')
#* '''1656-59''', ''Passíusálmar'' (''[[w:Passion Hymns|Passion Hymns]]''), hymn 1, verse 1 (orthography as in the [http://books.google.com/books?id=gvgOAAAAQAAJ&dq=%22hugur%20og%20tunga%20hj%C3%A1lpi%22&pg=PA5#v=onepage&q=%22hugur%20og%20tunga%20hj%C3%A1lpi%22&f=false 1887 printing]):
#*: Upp, upp, mín sál og allt mitt geð, <!--Up, up, my soul and all my thoughts,-->
#*: upp mitt hjarta og rómur með, <!--up my heart and ... -->
#*: hugur og tunga hjálpi til. 
#*: herrans pínu '''ég''' minnast vil.
#*:: ''translation by [http://books.google.com/books?id=QT3CjgeSOIEC&dq=%22up%2C%20up%20my%20soul%22%20%22and%20tongue%22&pg=PR7#v=onepage&q=%22up,%20up%20my%20soul%22%20%22and%20tongue%22&f=false William Charles Green]'':
#*::: Up, up, my soul and all my mind, 
#*::: Up, O my heart and voice combined; 
#*::: Help, thought and tongue; for '''I''' would fain 
#*::: Wake memory of our Lord's dear pain.
#*:: ''translation published in ''[http://books.google.com/books?id=j6c-AQAAIAAJ&q=%22up,+up+my+soul%22+%22and+tongue%22&dq=%22up,+up+my+soul%22+%22and+tongue%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=LmCYT-3YFM7y2gX0n4GfBw&ved=0CDkQ6AEwAQ Parergon]'', issues 1–13 (1971), page 31'':
#*::: Up, up my soul and all my mind, 
#*::: up my heart and voice as well. 
#*::: Thought and tongue help out. 
#*::: '''I''' intend to remember the Lord's suffering.
#* '''1800-1840''', [[w:Bjarni Thorarensen|Bjarni Thorarensen]], ''Solatium'':
#*: Kvíði '''ég''' ei dauða,
#*: konulaus maður,
#* '''2000''', [[w:Arnaldur Indriðason|Arnaldur Indriðason]], ''[[w:Mýrin|Mýrin]]'', page 59: 
#*: — Þekki '''ég''' þig? sagði hann. Um hvað ertu að tala? Hver ertu?
#*: — '''Ég''' heiti Erlendur. '''Ég''' er að rannsaka morð á manni að nafni Holberg í Reykjavík.
#*:: ''Jar City: A Reykjavík Thriller'', translation by Bernard Scudder:
#*::: "Do '''I''' know you?" he said. "What are you talking about? Who are you?" 
#*::: "My name’s [='''I''' am called] Erlendur. '''I'''’m investigating the murder of a man from Reykjavik by the name of Holberg."

